   "evidence": "The proof lines at Symbols.lean 253-256, 265-268, 321-324 and 333-336 are identical apart from `functionsIn`/`relationsIn` and `\u22a4`/`\u22a5`. The existing code factors the same pattern into a named helper: `CodedConnectives.lean:84 private theorem realize_pad \u2026 := Iff.of_eq (congrFun (c.comp_pad \u2026) k)`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/ModelTheory/Infinitary/Symbols.lean",
   "fix": "Add a lemma in `IndexCoding`, e.g. `iUnion_pad_of_eq_empty (c) {g : \u03b2 \u2192 Set \u03b3} {d} (hd : g d = \u2205) (f) : (\u22c3 k, g (c.pad d f k)) = \u22c3 i, g (f i)`, proved once from `comp_pad` and `exists_pad_false_iff`. Then close each of the four lemmas with `rw [iInfAlong_def/iSupAlong_def, functionsIn_iInf/\u2026, c.iUnion_pad_of_eq_empty functionsIn_top/\u2026]`.",
   "issue": "`functionsIn_iInfAlong` (248), `functionsIn_iSupAlong` (260), `relationsIn_iInfAlong` (316) and `relationsIn_iSupAlong` (328) each repeat the same 5-line proof. It pushes `IndexCoding.comp_pad` through `Iff.of_eq (congrArg (fun f => \u2203 k, f k) \u2026)` and `simpa only`, which hides the real step (the padding default contributes the empty set) and keeps a reusable fact out of the API.",
   "line": 248
  }
